[38;5;252m[1m## What I did[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mPhase A.[22m Built the C reference ([38;5;10mcmake[0m → [38;5;10mc_src/build/driver[0m) and the Rust binary ([38;5;10mcargo build --release[0m → [38;5;10mtranslation/target/release/driver[0m). Both compiled with zero errors and zero warnings; no compile fixes were needed.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mPhase B/C.[22m Read the C and enumerated every branch, then wrote [38;5;10mtranslation/tests/differential.rs[0m — 17 tests that spawn both binaries as subprocesses on identical stdin and compare stdout bytes, stderr bytes, exit code, and terminating signal. Roughly 3,000 comparisons in the suite; another ~28,000 ad-hoc ones during investigation (exhaustive 1–4 byte inputs over a strtol-relevant alphabet, ~5,500 random byte strings). All matched.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The branches that mattered:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mfgets[0m into [38;5;10mchar in[100][0m reads at most 99 bytes and stops at the first newline. Covered with a sweep across the 99/100-byte cutoff — the case that would silently pass on the happy path is 99 zeros followed by [38;5;10m9[0m, where truncation makes the value [38;5;10m0[0m, not [38;5;10m9[0m.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mparse_val[0m's three guards, each reached independently: no conversion ([38;5;10m"abc"[0m, [38;5;10m"-"[0m, [38;5;10m"- 5"[0m), [38;5;10mERANGE[0m (past [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m/[38;5;10mLONG_MIN[0m), and the [38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m/[38;5;10mINT_MAX[0m range rejections ([38;5;10m"2147483648"[0m, [38;5;10m"-2147483649"[0m).[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mstrtol[0m quirks that look like bugs and had to be preserved: [38;5;10m"0x1f"[0m succeeds returning [38;5;10m0[0m because [38;5;10mendp != str[0m; [38;5;10m"12abc"[0m and [38;5;10m"2.5"[0m succeed on the leading digits; an embedded NUL terminates the scan. glibc not setting [38;5;10merrno[0m on a failed conversion was confirmed empirically rather than assumed, since POSIX permits [38;5;10mEINVAL[0m there.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mthe_house[0m is a mutated global, so the second [38;5;10mrun(x)[0m continues from the first. [38;5;10mgolden_happy_path_exact_bytes[0m pins all eight output lines as literal bytes.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10madd_bedrooms[0m overflows [38;5;10mint[0m for large [38;5;10mx[0m; the Rust's [38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m matches. This is required, not stylistic — the release profile sets [38;5;10mpanic = "abort"[0m, so a plain [38;5;10m+=[0m would abort in debug builds.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mNegative control.[22m Because a suite that finds nothing is indistinguishable from a suite that tests nothing, I injected three bugs into [38;5;10mmain.rs[0m one at a time (widened range guard, off-by-one [38;5;10mfgets[0m capacity, [38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m → [38;5;10msaturating_add[0m). Each was caught; the source was then restored and verified byte-identical.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mPhase D.[22m Both build clean, [38;5;10mcargo test[0m passes in debug and release, no test is disabled or [38;5;10m#[ignore][0md, and [38;5;10mc_src/[0m is unmodified (only the expected [38;5;10mbuild/[0m directory was created).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## One caveat worth your attention[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mtranslation/ERRORS.md[0m records the full branch enumeration plus one residual divergence I could not eliminate: Rust's runtime sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m, while the C inherits the default. If stdout were a pipe whose reader closed before the ~450 bytes flushed, the C could die with status 141 where the Rust exits 0. My direct test had both exit 0 because the output is small enough to be delivered first, and no stdin input can trigger it — but a sufficiently adversarial harness could. Fixing it needs a [38;5;10mlibc[0m dependency the crate does not have, so I left it documented rather than adding one unasked.[0m[0m
